## 🌟 About the Project

This project is a simple **Library Management System** created using **Dart**.

The main purpose of this project is to understand and apply basic Dart programming and **Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)** concepts in a real-world example.

The program stores books, displays their details, and allows a book to be borrowed.

---

## 🎯 Objectives

- Understand Dart programming basics
- Use variables and lists
- Use loops and functions
- Understand classes and objects
- Implement constructors
- Understand inheritance
- Create a simple real-world console application

---

## 🧩 Concepts Used

| Concept | Purpose |
|---|---|
| 🔤 Variables | Store student and book information |
| 📚 List | Store multiple book objects |
| 🔄 Loop | Display books one by one |
| ⚙️ Function | Perform the borrowing operation |
| 🏗️ Class | Create the structure of a book |
| 🔧 Constructor | Initialize book details |
| 📦 Object | Create individual books |
| 🌳 Inheritance | `EBook` inherits from `Book` |

